1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,065
Action Receipt turns one notice into actions you can check.

2
00:00:04,065 --> 00:00:09,600
This walkthrough shows real program outputs, not a recording of the
browser interface.

3
00:00:11,350 --> 00:00:15,325
This invented school notice separates registration from payment.

4
00:00:15,325 --> 00:00:21,995
It also includes a consent form, a conditional transport request,
and a fee that is explicitly waived.

5
00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:29,360
The local rules propose three actions and flag two passages.

6
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,700
Nothing is approved automatically.

7
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:35,750
At this point, neither download includes any tasks or events.

8
00:00:37,350 --> 00:00:42,690
Registration and the bus deposit keep their own deadlines and exact
source quotations.

9
00:00:42,690 --> 00:00:47,350
The words are traceable, but a person must still check their
interpretation.

10
00:00:48,350 --> 00:00:51,260
The rules missed the consent instruction.

11
00:00:51,260 --> 00:00:55,605
The repair function uses the flagged passage to create a separate
action.

12
00:00:55,605 --> 00:00:59,185
Its date stays unresolved and its approval stays unchecked.

13
00:01:00,350 --> 00:01:03,995
The waived membership fee is marked as not an obligation.

14
00:01:03,995 --> 00:01:09,375
That decision preserves its reason without creating another task or
calendar event.

15
00:01:10,350 --> 00:01:13,555
Accessible transport applies only if needed.

16
00:01:13,555 --> 00:01:16,525
The phrase next Friday stays unresolved.

17
00:01:16,525 --> 00:01:20,665
The program does not invent a calendar date or remove the condition.

18
00:01:22,350 --> 00:01:24,970
These review choices are scripted checks.

19
00:01:24,970 --> 00:01:30,320
Approving four actions produces four checklist tasks, but zero
calendar entries.

20
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:34,410
Confirming the two complete dates then enables two calendar entries.

21
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:38,680
This excerpt comes from the actual checklist file.

22
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:42,290
Each approved action keeps its source quotation.

23
00:01:42,290 --> 00:01:47,555
The consent form and conditional email remain checklist tasks
without calendar dates.

24
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:52,345
The calendar file contains only two entries.

25
00:01:52,345 --> 00:01:54,760
Registration is an all day marker.

26
00:01:54,760 --> 00:02:00,745
The deposit cutoff converts from five P M, U T C minus ten, to the
same instant in U T C.

27
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:06,555
Editing the reviewed cutoff clears approval and date confirmation.

28
00:02:06,555 --> 00:02:10,050
Opening a saved review also requires fresh checks.

29
00:02:10,050 --> 00:02:13,720
Earlier decisions never silently authorize a new download.

30
00:02:15,350 --> 00:02:21,530
Codex used the Devpost Learn Skill Pack, with generated planning
documents in the public repository.

31
00:02:21,530 --> 00:02:27,405
The finished app runs local rules, without model downloads,
accounts, or A P I credits.

32
00:02:28,350 --> 00:02:33,625
Source and the offline browser app are on GitHub under nolankido,
action receipt.

33
00:02:33,625 --> 00:02:35,860
This supporting walkthrough is complete.

34
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:40,785
Actual browser footage and a public video link are still needed for
the submission demo.
